On Nov 27, 6:29 am, Justin <JustinTNel...@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Nov 26, 9:47 pm, Carl <carlhnel...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> > Does anyone here know what the effect on Hp and Pw is for a polyself
> > to the same race?
> > For example, if I lose a level due to a same-race polyself, is my HP/
> > PW rerolled as though I was a new character, or do I only lose the HP/
> > PW associated with the change in level?
>
> Short answer: you gain/lose HP based on the level change.
>
> Accurate answer:
>
> Quoth the source,
>   u.uhpmax = ((u.uhpmax - 10) * (long)u.ulevel / oldlvl + 10) +
>   (9 - rn2(19));
>
> In other words, it adjusts your HP proportional to your change in
> level, but sets aside the first 10 HP. And then it adds or subtracts
> up to 9.
>
> So if you have 60 HP at level 5, and you lose two levels from polyself
> (ouch), you lose roughly 20 maxHP.
>
> > What about the extra HP gained from wight dancing, b!oFH, or nurse
> > dancing, etc.?  A reroll would erase those gains while a subtraction
> > would only take away the HP gained from the level(s) lost.
>
> You'll not only keep those extra hit points, but you'll get bonus HP
> because of the proportional change -- or if you lost levels, you get a
> "bonus" HP loss, but your hard alchemy work is not all lost.  e.g. if
> you're level 20 with 510 HP, and you polyself down two levels, you
> lose 50 (+-9) hit points.

